        <mxCell id="c34" value="" style="rounded=0;html=1;fillColor=#e67e22;strokeColor=#e67e22;opacity=40;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="165.0" y="950.0" width="40.0" height="22.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c35" value="&lt;b&gt;Good-sound band&lt;/b&gt; of speaker A (blue) and B (orange): ±30° around each speaker's axis (LP-6 V2 listening window, flat response). The LP-6 is specified for 120° coverage, so up to ±60° is still usable but gets duller. &lt;b&gt;Darker overlap = stereo sweet zone.&lt;/b&gt; Speakers are toed-in towards the centre of the group." style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="215.0" y="940.0" width="565.0" height="60.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c36" value="&lt;b&gt;Evaluation of your idea (v4)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; I read your sketch as rotated by 180° (couch bottom-left = north-east corner, Schrank on the east wall) and redrew it to scale. Controllers are assumed to sit together as one 60 × 80 cm block at the east end of the table.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; &lt;table border=&quot;1&quot; cellpadding=&quot;4&quot; style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:11px;&quot;&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Metric&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Your idea&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;v3&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Max distance between players&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;1.30 m&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;1.01 m&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Avg distance between players&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0.94 m&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;0.75 m&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;All 4 reach all 3 controllers (≤ 0.75 m)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;yes*&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;yes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Speaker distance / spacing&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;1.4 m / 1.25 m&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;2.4 m / 0.9 m&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Stereo angle at group centre (ideal ≈ 60°)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;54°&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;19°&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;All players inside both ±30° bands&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;yes (max 28°)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;yes (max 12°)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/table&gt; * only with the compact block at the east end. Spread along the 1.8 m table, the long-side players would not reach everything.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; &lt;b&gt;Pros:&lt;/b&gt; a natural ring with eye contact; the table end on the wall saves floor space and keeps the door lane free; speakers close by form a proper stereo triangle on the group; all four stand inside the good-sound band of both speakers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; &lt;b&gt;Cons:&lt;/b&gt; players on opposite long sides can never be closer than 1.30 m (table depth + body), so the max distance is 29 % worse than v3; P1 and P4 are at the full 0.75 m stretch to the far XL3; only P1/P4 can reach the MacBook; P2/P3 have the speakers behind them and P1/P4 to the side, so nobody faces the speakers (stereo image shifts when they turn). P1 and P4 sit near the edge of the bands (28°), still well inside the 60° coverage.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; &lt;b&gt;Verdict:&lt;/b&gt; good if the stereo image and sociability matter; v3 wins if max/average distance is the top priority. Tilt the LP-6 down, they sit at ~2.3 m height." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fillColor=#f9f9f9;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="830.0" y="120.0" width="440.0" height="740.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
